---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';

const entries = [
  {
    date: 'November 2026',
    title: 'Closed testing begins',
    body: 'Version 1.0.0 is in closed testing on Google Play. The reader is complete enough to read with: EPUB, PDF, MOBI, CBZ, TTS, highlights, bookmarks and an OPDS catalogue browser. It is not complete enough to call finished, which is why the testing track exists.',
  },
  {
    date: 'November 2026',
    title: 'The paid-app entry was removed',
    body: 'An inherited menu entry opened a different, paid reader by the upstream author, labelled with our own name. It is gone, together with the settings row and the method behind it. No path in the app now leads to a purchase.',
  },
  {
    date: 'November 2026',
    title: 'Folders stopped being called Librera',
    body: 'The rebrand missed paths built by string concatenation: the sync folder, the TTS scratch folder and the stylesheet name still carried the old name into the visible file system. They now read OmniShelf.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Shelf — what is on it, and what changed"
  description="The state of the OmniShelf reader: closed testing on Google Play, what is finished, what is not, and a short changelog of the decisions that altered it."
>
  <div class="shell">
    <Prose>
      <p class="meta">Shelf</p>
      <h1>What is on the shelf</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        One app, in closed testing. This page is the honest state of it — what works,
        what does not yet, and what changed recently. It is not a feature list; the store
        listing has that.
      </p>

      <h2>The app</h2>
      <p>
        OmniShelf for Android, version 1.0.0, is in closed testing on Google Play. When
        the testing period ends it will be published publicly, free, with no advertising
        and no purchases. If you are one of the testers, install through the invitation
        link you were sent rather than searching the store — a closed track is invisible
        to search until it opens.
      </p>
      <p>
        The source is public and the licence is the AGPLv3:
        <a href="https://github.com/tt7247129-sys/omnishelf" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
          >github.com/tt7247129-sys/omnishelf</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>What works today</h2>
      <p>
        Opening and reading EPUB, PDF, MOBI, AZW3, FB2, DJVU, CBZ/CBR, DOCX, ODT, RTF,
        Markdown, HTML and plain text. A single library that mixes them. Reading progress
        that survives a restart. Highlights, notes, bookmarks, text-to-speech with the
        device voice, and OPDS catalogue browsing. Night mode, adjustable margins, spacing
        and alignment.
      </p>

      <h2>What is not finished</h2>
      <p>
        Cloud sync is not offered, deliberately: it would require an account, and an
        account would mean the app holds something about you. Widget behaviour on unusual
        launchers is untested. Some right-to-left layouts still break on the two-page
        mode. These are recorded here rather than discovered by a reviewer.
      </p>
    </Prose>

    <hr />

    <Prose>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
    </Prose>
    <ul class="note-list">
      {entries.map((entry) => (
        <li>
          <article class="entry">
            <p class="meta">{entry.date}</p>
            <h3>{entry.title}</h3>
            <p>{entry.body}</p>
          </article>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .entry {
    padding: var(--space-4) 0;
  }

  .entry h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .entry p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
